<section class="hero">
  <h1><span class="accent">Schema</span>Flux</h1>
  <p class="tagline">A compiler for structured data</p>

  <div class="terminal">
    <code><span class="prompt">$ </span>go install github.com/greynewell/schemaflux/cmd/schemaflux@latest</code>
  </div>

  <p class="stats">
    <span class="highlight">1,997 entities &rarr; 2,328 pages in ~500ms</span>
    <span class="separator">&middot;</span>
    Zero dependencies. Single binary.
  </p>

  <div class="cta-group">
    <a href="/docs/quick-start/" class="btn btn-primary">Get Started</a>
    <a href="{{ site.repo_url }}" class="btn btn-secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="features">
  <div class="feature-card">
    <h3>Compiler Pipeline</h3>
    <p>12 ordered passes transform your data from markdown to output. Each pass enriches the intermediate representation with computed metadata.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-card">
    <h3>Pluggable Backends</h3>
    <p>Built-in HTML backend with taxonomy pages, JSON-LD, sitemaps, RSS, pagination, A-Z indices, and search.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-card">
    <h3>Zero Dependencies</h3>
    <p>Go standard library only. Compiles to a single static binary. No runtime, no node_modules, no Docker needed.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-card">
    <h3>Structured Data</h3>
    <p>JSON-LD schemas, Open Graph tags, XML sitemaps, RSS feeds, robots.txt, and llms.txt generated automatically.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<h2>Documentation</h2>

{% set sections = {} %}
{% for doc in collections.docs %}
  {% set sec = doc.data.section or "General" %}
